e penitentiary the largest maximum  security prison in the nation where at  sunset vincent simmons walked out oh  yeah  of the place he has been held in since  he was 25 years old hey man  the judge said on the bench yesterday i  want to be clear i'm not telling you  that vincent simmons is guilty or  innocent i'm just telling you he  deserves a new trial when the district  attorney stood up almost immediately and  said judge we're not going to retry him  that meant the charges at that moment  were dropped when vincent walked out of  here last night he said he wanted a  crawfish dinner so he got it  what's next for him  he says he wants to leave louisiana and  start again somewhere else  wow wow well david we can certainly  understand that uh congratulations to  you and your team for a lot of hard work  here there were a lot of people involved  working on this case for a lot of years  to to bring vincent simmons into the  outside world as a free man you  mentioned he's free but not exonerated  so i do have a question first of all who  met him there he was hugging two uh  ladies and there were some cheers i'm  curious who was there and also is there  any hope of restitution for the 44 years  he paid for a crime he says he didn't  commit  his sisters and his attorney met him  here and there is hope but it's going to  be hard the d.a said he would  essentially have to go to what is a  trial and convince a judge that he can  prove his innocence proving that he's  innocent may be difficult but when you  say that he had a lot of help tony it's  important to note every attorney who  helped him was simply using the  information that vincent had obtained  himself nobody believed vincent when he  stood up in front of a judge by himself  but he kept trying he kept trying and  was expecting to die here in prison  but instead  after 44 years he won  and the tragedy is david there are so  many more vincent simmons out there  david we thank you so much for this  incredible gift that you've given  to  the simmons family  and to cbs news

